function rulesHTML() {
  return `<section class="rules-page"><span class="eyebrow">FIELD MANUAL</span><h1>Know your arena.</h1><div class="rules-grid"><article><h2>The battle</h2><p>Destroy the enemy King Tower for an immediate three-crown victory, or take more towers before time expires. Each outer tower is one crown.</p><p>Regulation lasts 3 minutes. Ties enter 2 minutes of sudden death. At five minutes, the side with the higher lowest remaining tower HP wins; equal HP is a draw.</p><h2>Your hand & elixir</h2><p>Build a deck of 8 unique cards. Four are in your hand, with the next card visible. Playing a card rotates it to the back of your queue. Start with 5 elixir and hold up to 10.</p><p>Elixir doubles after 2 minutes and triples in the final minute of overtime. Troops deploy after 1 second. Ground troops use bridges; flyers cross the river, and Hog Rider jumps it.</p><h2>Bot Ladder</h2><p>Wins award 30 trophies; losses remove up to 30, stopping at your highest reached gate: 0, 300, 600, 900 or 1200. Draws never change trophies. Above 1200, wins keep adding trophies in the Champion Circuit. Stone Keep opens at 300 trophies with a stone courtyard, a permanent 300-trophy gate and tougher bots that defend and counterpush more effectively. Higher arenas retain the stronger tactics with faster reactions.</p><p>Every opponent is a bot with the same levels and elixir rules. Bots see public battlefield units and their own hand, but cannot read your hand, queue, or exact elixir. The bot builds its deck from your unlocked collection.</p></article><article><h2>Cards & progression</h2><p>New saves start with eight cards. Unlock twelve more through Trophy Road. Claim a Card Key on Trophy Road at 300, 480, 780, 1080 and 1200 trophies. These are separate from the original road rewards, so previously reached milestones still offer their unclaimed Keys. The ten Key-exclusive cards cost one Card Key each, at any trophy count. Card Keys can only be spent on these ten cards. Existing unlocks are kept.</p><p>Heroes and Evolutions are removed. All eight deck slots accept standard cards. Archer Queen remains a Champion with a single-use, 3.5-second Cloaking Cape ability.</p><h2>Pass Royale</h2><p>Each free Crown Journey has 30 tiers, one per 10 Crowns. Earn Crowns for towers destroyed and your towers left standing, plus objective bonuses. Some tiers offer a reward choice. Claim all tiers to begin the next journey; there is no expiry.</p><p>Conceded battles give no Gold, Crowns or objective progress. Trophy losses still apply. Rewards already claimed and card unlocks are permanent.</p><h2>Collection Book & Shop</h2><p>The Collection Book has eight permanent card sets. Own every card in a set to claim its Gold and Gems once. Earlier card unlocks count; rewards have no expiry. Find the book on Home, in the Shop or in your profile.</p><p>The Shop has 25 banner decorations, 10 frames, three permanent banner/frame bundles and two emote bundles. Search the catalogue and filter by item type, ownership and affordability; price sorting groups Gold and Gems separately. Bundles cost 20% less than buying their missing items separately, rounded up; owned items are excluded from the price. All items are cosmetic and purchases use earned Gold or Gems.</p><h2>Cosmetic Challenges & Card Mastery</h2><p>Seven permanent challenges award banners, frames, emotes, titles and badges. Card Mastery tracks plays and wins using each of the 30 cards across Bronze, Silver and Gold tiers. Only completed bot battles with a card played count; conceded and friendly battles do not. Tracking starts with this update. Claim earned rewards, then choose your title, badge and unlocked favourite card in Customise Profile. These rewards do not change card stats or trophies.</p><h2>Emotes</h2><p>Four King emotes are free. Purchase original Crownfall emotes with Gold or Gems in the Shop, or earn selected originals through permanent cosmetic challenges, then equip up to eight in Emote Collection. Emote purchases never spend Card Keys. Open the speech bubble in a bot or friendly battle to send an equipped emote; there is a 2.5-second cooldown. You can mute emotes and choose Small, Medium or Large bubbles in Settings. The Below arena picker opens over the card tray. Reduced-motion settings keep the artwork still. Emote ownership and equipped slots are included in your save backup.</p><h2>Controls</h2><p><b>Mouse or touch:</b> select a card, then tap the arena, or drag a card to deploy. Click an ability to activate it.</p><p><b>Keyboard:</b> 1–4 select a card; arrow keys move the targeting cursor; Enter deploys; Escape cancels or pauses; Q activates Archer Queen’s available ability.</p><p>Changing tabs pauses your match. Return to resume. Progress and interrupted battles are saved locally.</p><p><b>Immersion controls:</b> use the sound button beside your hand, the emote button inside the arena, or pause and open Settings for music, effects and haptics. Full screen is available from the top bar in supported browsers.</p></article><article class="adaptation-note"><h2>About this adaptation</h2><p>Crownfall Arena implements the 30-card collection with Clash Royale card, troop and tower artwork alongside an original battle arena and authentic lobby artwork. It is an independent fan-inspired prototype, not an official Supercell game or a verified 1:1 copy.</p><p>Standard cards use a researched Level 11 balance snapshot dated September 14, 2026. Existing saved battles retain their original stats. Pathfinding, bot strategy, targeting details, Champion behavior, visuals, and progression are adaptations. Friends mode offers free direct browser battles through a private invite and reply exchange. Both players must use the same game file and keep it open. After a completed friendly, stay connected to change decks and confirm a rematch; both players must tap Ready. Connections can fail on restrictive networks; there is no relay. Friendly matches have no trophies, currency, Crown Rewards, ladder records or replays, and cannot resume after interruption. Friend contacts save locally and are not verified accounts. There are no real-money purchases, card upgrades, or account synchronization. The Shop and crown reward track are local adaptations: earned Gold and Gems buy banner decorations, frames and Card Keys. The daily gift and each guaranteed shop offer reset at 00:00 UTC; purchases use this device’s saved currency. The five saved decks stay in this browser.</p><p>Clash Royale artwork © Supercell, sourced through <a href="https://github.com/RoyaleAPI/cr-api-assets" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RoyaleAPI</a>, the <a href="https://github.com/smlbiobot/cr-assets-png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">game sprite archive</a>, and <a href="https://fankit.supercell.com/d/BmehSDJrZNff/game-assets-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Supercell Fankit</a>. This content is not affiliated with, endorsed, sponsored, or specifically approved by Supercell.</p><p>Rules snapshot: September 14, 2026 · ${_data.RULES}. Saves stay on this device. Open Menu → Save Data to download, share, copy or restore a verified backup.</p></article></div></section>`;
